Specification AddressCorrection
Description Standardizes street addresses through the address correction API

# An illustration of testing a business-defined API. There are no production
# classes: the API is the thing under test. The glue turns each table into JSON
# with the generated toJSON(), calls the service, turns the response back with
# the generated fromJsonValue(), and compares -- the same three jobs as
# API_glue.java in SpecStudioVariousTests, over the same RestCall helper.
#
# The URL is built from three parts: the base Page below, the scenario's Page,
# and its Parameter.
#
# This is what an API specification looks like when every expected value is a
# real one. "1 Penny LN" becomes "1 Penny Lane" or the service is wrong, and the
# table says which. Nothing here is a type placeholder.

Background
Given base Page is : String
| https://api.example.com/address |

# ============================================================
# The abbreviation the caller typed is expanded
# ============================================================

Scenario Expand a street suffix
When sending request : Request Vertical
| Method | POST     |
| Page   | correct  |
| Body   | Submitted |
And submitted address is : Submitted Vertical
| Street | 1 Penny LN |
| City   | Liverpool  |
| State  | NY         |
| Zip    | 13088      |
Then response status is : Status Vertical
| Code | 200 |
And response body is : Corrected Vertical
| Street  | 1 Penny Lane |
| City    | Liverpool    |
| State   | NY           |
| Zip     | 13088        |
| Quality | Verified     |

# LN -> Lane is the whole point of the call, so it is stated as a literal. A
# cell reading "string" here would pass whatever the service returned.

# ============================================================
# Several corrections at once
# ============================================================

Scenario Expand a directional, a suffix and a unit
When sending request : Request Vertical
| Method | POST      |
| Page   | correct   |
| Body   | Submitted |
And submitted address is : Submitted Vertical
| Street | 100 n main st apt 4b |
| City   | springfield          |
| State  | il                   |
| Zip    | 62701                |
Then response status is : Status Vertical
| Code | 200 |
And response body is : Corrected Vertical
| Street  | 100 North Main Street Apartment 4B |
| City    | Springfield                        |
| State   | IL                                 |
| Zip     | 62701-1032                         |
| Quality | Verified                           |

# The Zip gained its +4 from the correction. That is a business rule worth
# pinning: the caller sent five digits and is entitled to nine back.

# ============================================================
# Only some fields matter
# ============================================================

# CompareOnly checks the columns shown and ignores every other field of
# Corrected. Use it when the scenario is about one rule -- here, that a PO Box
# is recognised whatever else comes back.

Scenario Recognize a post office box
When sending request : Request Vertical
| Method | POST      |
| Page   | correct   |
| Body   | Submitted |
And submitted address is : Submitted Vertical
| Street | po box 12 |
| City   | Liverpool |
| State  | NY        |
| Zip    | 13088     |
Then response status is : Status Vertical
| Code | 200 |
And response body is : Corrected CompareOnly
| Street         | Quality  |
| PO Box 12      | Verified |

# A step takes one modifier, so CompareOnly cannot be written with Vertical.
# The table is horizontal instead -- which is also how several rows are checked
# at once.

# ============================================================
# The address cannot be corrected
# ============================================================

Scenario Reject an address that does not exist
When sending request : Request Vertical
| Method | POST      |
| Page   | correct   |
| Body   | Submitted |
And submitted address is : Submitted Vertical
| Street | 9999 Nowhere Rd |
| City   | Liverpool       |
| State  | NY              |
| Zip    | 13088           |
Then response status is : Status Vertical
| Code | 200 |
And response body is : Corrected Vertical
| Street  | ?DNC?      |
| City    | ?DNC?      |
| State   | ?DNC?      |
| Zip     | ?DNC?      |
| Quality | Unverified |

# A failure to correct is still a 200 -- the call succeeded, the address did
# not. ?DNC? says the corrected fields are deliberately not checked here rather
# than forgotten.

# ============================================================
# Ambiguity returns candidates
# ============================================================

Scenario Return every candidate for an ambiguous street
When sending request : Request Vertical
| Method | POST      |
| Page   | candidates |
| Body   | Submitted |
And submitted address is : Submitted Vertical
| Street | 1 Penny  |
| City   | Liverpool |
| State  | NY        |
| Zip    | 13088     |
Then response status is : Status Vertical
| Code | 200 |
And response array items match : Corrected CompareOnly
| Street         |
| 1 Penny Lane   |
| 1 Penny Court  |

# Two rows, checked against the array the service returned, on Street alone.
# Every other field of Corrected is ?DNC?, so adding a field to the response
# does not break this scenario.

# ============================================================
# Look up a previous correction by its identifier
# ============================================================

Scenario Retrieve a stored correction
When sending request : Request Vertical
| Method    | GET       |
| Page      | correction |
| Parameter | 4471      |
Then response status is : Status Vertical
| Code | 200 |
And response body is : Corrected Vertical
| Street  | 1 Penny Lane |
| City    | Liverpool    |
| State   | NY           |
| Zip     | 13088        |
| Quality | Verified     |

Scenario Report an identifier that is not stored
When sending request : Request Vertical
| Method    | GET        |
| Page      | correction |
| Parameter | 999999     |
Then response status is : Status Vertical
| Code | 404 |

Attributes Request
| Attribute | Type   | Default | Notes                                         |
| Method    | String |         | GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE                 |
| Page      | String |         | Appended to the base Page from the Background |
| Parameter | String |         | Appended after the Page, such as an id        |
| Body      | String |         | Name of the attribute set holding the body    |

Attributes Status
| Attribute | Type    | Default | Notes            |
| Code      | Integer | 200     | HTTP status code |

Attributes Submitted
| Attribute | Type   | Default | Notes                       |
| Street    | String |         | As the caller typed it      |
| City      | String |         |                             |
| State     | String |         | Two letters, any case       |
| Zip       | String |         | Five digits or ZIP+4        |

Attributes Corrected
| Attribute | Type    | Default | Notes                            |
| Street    | String  |         | Suffixes and directionals spelled out |
| City      | String  |         | Title case                       |
| State     | String  |         | Two upper case letters           |
| Zip       | String  |         | ZIP+4 where the service knows it |
| Quality   | Quality |         | Whether the address was found    |

DataType Quality
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value      | Notes                                            |
| Verified   | The address exists and was standardized          |
| Unverified | No matching address; the corrected fields are unset |
